// Title: PUA - DefenderCheck Execution
// Sigma ID: f0ca6c24-3225-47d5-b1f5-352bf07ecfa7
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-30 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1027.005
// Description: Detects the use of DefenderCheck, a tool to evaluate the signatures used in Microsoft Defender.
//   It can be used to figure out the strings / byte chains used in Microsoft Defender to detect a
//   tool and thus used for AV evasion.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/matterpreter/DefenderCheck
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_pua_defendercheck.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\DefenderCheck.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription =~ "DefenderCheck"
